{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeInclInjective","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeInclInjective","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeProductInjective","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalBlockEquality","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.YoungDiagramEraseCornerSurjective"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.heckeIncl_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.heckeIncl_injective","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeInclInjective.lean#L87-L92","doc":"**The tower inclusion is injective.** `H_m(q) ↪ H_{m+1}(q)` at generic `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.seminormalRep_eq_of_heckeIncl_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SeminormalRep.seminormalRep_eq_of_heckeIncl_eq","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeInclInjective.lean#L72-L85","doc":"**Step 3, first half.** If the tower inclusion identifies `x` and `y`, then so does every\ndownstairs seminormal block — at an *arbitrary* diagram of the right size. The diagram is a\nvariable so that `exists_eraseCorner_eq` can be `subst`ed into it; see the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}